        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 304.11,
          "end": 305.363,
          "en": "for incrementing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 306.79,
          "end": 308.96,
          "en": "Now this was forbidden before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 308.96,
          "end": 312.06,
          "en": "and I emphasized that it is forbidden.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 312.06,
          "end": 316.37,
          "en": "I also did emphasize it because here it seems to be allowed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 316.37,
          "end": 319.83,
          "en": "But the important part is the word seems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 319.83,
          "end": 324.1,
          "en": "We still must not manipulate the existing state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 324.1,
          "end": 327.67,
          "en": "but the good thing is when using Redux toolkit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 327.67,
          "end": 330.41,
          "en": "and its functions like create slice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 330.41,
          "end": 334.54,
          "en": "we can't accidentally manipulate the existing state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 334.54,
          "end": 338.76,
          "en": "Because Redux toolkit internally uses another package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 338.76,
          "end": 342.65999999999997,
          "en": "called imgur, which will detect code like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 342.65999999999997,
          "end": 346.92,
          "en": "and which will automatically clone the existing state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 346.92,
          "end": 350.84000000000003,
          "en": "create a new state object, keep all the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 350.84000000000003,
          "end": 354.38,
          "en": "which we're not editing, and override the state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 354.38,
          "end": 358.22,
          "en": "which we are editing in an immutable way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 358.22,
          "end": 360.95,
          "en": "So we still have immutable code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 360.95,
          "end": 362.92,
          "en": "even though it doesn't look like it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 362.92,
          "end": 366.83,
          "en": "because of this internally used package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 366.83,
          "end": 369.16,
          "en": "and therefore we as a developer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 369.16,
          "end": 371.85,
          "en": "have a much easier time working with Redux",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 371.85,
          "end": 374.68,
          "en": "because we don't have to create a copy manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 374.68,
          "end": 377.46,
          "en": "and keep all the code we're not changing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 377.46,
          "end": 380.38,
          "en": "instead, we just change the code we wanna change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 380.38,
          "end": 384.743,
          "en": "and internally it's translated into immutable code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 386.16,
          "end": 389.617,
          "en": "Therefore in decrement we execute state.counter--",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 390.97,
          "end": 393.01,
          "en": "and here for increase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 393.01,
          "end": 395.24,
          "en": "we now need a payload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 395.24,
          "end": 398.01,
          "en": "We now need extra data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 398.01,
          "end": 400,
          "en": "So how does that work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 400,
          "end": 403.34000000000003,
          "en": "Now when using Redux toolkit we of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 403.34000000000003,
          "end": 407.65,
          "en": "can still have reducers that listen to actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 407.65,
          "end": 411.21,
          "en": "that have an extra payload, extra data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 411.21,
          "end": 413.36,
          "en": "Because these were user functions here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 413.36,
